## 📦 Environment & Dependencies (uv)

`uv` (Astral, Rust) is the environment + dependency manager — it replaces pip, venv, pyenv,
and pip-tools with one fast binary, and is the 2026 default. `pyproject.toml` is the single
source of truth; **no `requirements.txt` anywhere**.

```bash
uv init                     # scaffold pyproject.toml
uv add polars pydantic pydantic-settings structlog stamina    # runtime deps
uv add pandas openpyxl                    # retained boundaries only (templates, plotting)
uv add --optional excel fastexcel         # Polars' calamine reader for .xlsx ingestion
uv add --dev pytest ruff mypy deepeval   # dev-only → [dependency-groups]
uv sync                     # reproduce the exact locked env on any machine
uv sync --frozen            # CI/Docker: fail if the lock is stale, never re-resolve
uv run pytest               # run inside the env (no manual activate)
```

- **Commit `uv.lock`** — it pins exact versions/hashes for reproducible installs.
- Dev tools go in `[dependency-groups]`, keeping runtime deps lean.
- `uv run <cmd>` auto-activates the env; no `source .venv/bin/activate` needed.

> ⏸️ **Conda exception — one project only.** Conda earns a place in **Crucible only**, and
> only if it grows heavy numerical / CUDA / C++ (BLAS/compiled) backends where its binary
> channels resolve compiled scientific stacks more cleanly than wheels. Every other project
> stays uv-only.

