## 🚀 CI Pipeline (GitHub Actions)

Every project ships CI. The lint / type / test / eval sequence is **merge-blocking** via
a branch protection rule on `main`.

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml
name: CI Pipeline
on: [push, pull_request]

jobs:
  quality:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Install uv
        uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@v5
        with:
          enable-cache: true

      - name: Set up Python
        run: uv python install 3.12

      - name: Install locked dependencies
        run: uv sync --frozen          # fails if uv.lock is stale — never re-resolves

      - name: Lint
        run: uv run ruff check src/ tests/

      - name: Format check
        run: uv run ruff format --check src/ tests/

      - name: Type check
        run: uv run mypy src/

      - name: Test
        run: uv run pytest tests/ -v --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing

      - name: AI evaluation (blocking gate)
        run: uv run deepeval test run tests/test_eval.py
        env:
          DEEPEVAL_MODEL: ${{ vars.DEEPEVAL_JUDGE }}
          ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}
```

- **No `pip install ".[dev]"`** — that path predates the uv standard and bypasses the lock.
- Cache uv, not pip.
- The eval job is a gate, not a report. See `testing-and-eval.mdc`.
